    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d153">

                <pb facs="0202" n="194" sameAs="frus:frus1938v02/pg194"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">841D.513/51</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in the Irish
                        Free State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Cudahy</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 7</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-10-04">October 4, 1937</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I enclose a copy of a letter dated August
                    20, 1936, from the Acting Postmaster General,<anchor n="15" xml:id="d153-f1"/>
                    together with its enclosures, in regard to the desire of the Post Office
                    Department to acquaint the Irish Free State Government with violations of United
                    States statutes which are being practiced by the Hospitals’ Trust, Limited.</p>
                <p>You are requested to take up this matter with the appropriate authorities and to
                    request that steps be taken to prevent further violations of United States
                    statutes.</p>
                <p>For your information I enclose a copy of the Department’s recent communication to
                    the Postmaster General on this matter.<anchor n="16" xml:id="d153-f2"/></p>
                <p>Very truly yours,</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hugh R.
                            Wilson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d153-f1" n="15" xml:id="d153-f1-content">
                <p>Not attached to file copy of instruction.</p>
            </note>
